      "hint": "When the problem never says which quantity the public number is, that role is itself unknown to the speakers: keep every reading alive in one candidate table rather than committing up front. Let a candidate be (my number, other number, role). Group candidates by the value a speaker privately holds; \"I don't know\" means that group still holds two or more possibilities, so delete size-one groups. Discard a reading only if it dies for every private value, not merely for one. Apply announcements in chronological order, regrouping after each deletion. If you keep re-deriving one contradiction, your state is missing a hidden variable: add it instead of guessing.",
