      "train_qid": "8554",
      "hint": "Union = sum of areas minus overlap, so maximize the union by minimizing overlap. Before optimizing over the angle, test whether the overlap is angle-independent. Criterion: if the shared point is a center of k-fold rotational symmetry of one shape, and the other shape meets it as a wedge of angle 2*pi/k whose two edges reach past that shape (so only those rays cut it), then the k rotated copies of the wedge tile around the point and cut the symmetric shape into k congruent pieces, so the overlap is the same fraction 1/k at every angle. Verify by computing the overlap at one aligned and one skewed orientation; if they match, that value is both the minimum and maximum, so skip calculus and case analysis, report the union, and stop. Build a piecewise area function only if the two test values disagree.",
