      "train_position": 189,
      "train_qid": "25003",
      "hint": "When each term of the required pattern may come from any of N given functions, never compare adjacent terms: neighbours can use different functions, so that route yields no bound. Write the pattern's value at index n as an explicit T(n), then partition indices by which function produced them. On one function P's group, P - T vanishes and is not identically zero, since subtracting the low-degree T cannot cancel P's leading term; so that group holds at most deg P indices. Hence Bound = N x deg P. Trust that product even if it looks too large for a contest; do not shrink or re-derive it. Instead verify by construction: give each function its own block of consecutive indices and interpolate T's values there - matching that many points leaves coefficients free, so a legal function exists. Bound plus construction is the whole proof; then answer.",
