      "hint": "Fit unknown parameters first: rewrite each given point in exponential form (log_c u = y means u = c^y) and solve the resulting system. For the unknown vertices, use the vector condition to write one as a translation of a variable point, then subtract the two log equations so only a ratio of arguments survives: a y-difference d becomes argument factor c^d. With base under 1 this inverts the naive direction, so test that ratio relation on the known points before solving. A negative discriminant, or roots outside the domain, means an orientation, sign, or branch choice is wrong: flip it and redo once instead of re-verifying the same arithmetic. Get the area as the absolute cross product of adjacent edge vectors.",
